w: O for a thou- sand tongues to sing My great Re- deem- er's praise,
w: My gra- cious Mas- ter and my God, A- ssist me to pro- claim,
w: Je- sus! the name that charms our fears, That bids our sor- rows cease;
w: He breaks the pow'r of can- celed sin, He sets the pri- soner free;
w: He speaks, and, lis- tening to His voice, New life the dead re- ceive,
w: Glo- ry to God, and praise and love Be ev- er, ev- er giv'n,
w: On this glad day the glo- rious Sun Of Right- eous- ness a- rose;
w: Then with my heart I first be- lieved, Be- lieved with faith di- vine,
w: I felt my Lord's a- to- ning blood Close to my soul ap- plied;
w: I found and owned His pro- mise true, As- cer- tained of my part,
w: Look un- to Him, ye na- tions, own Your God, ye fal- len race;
w: Har- lots and pub- li- cans and thieves In ho- ly tri- umph join!
e2 | e c c2 A2 | A F F2 (A F) | E A A2 B2 | A4 |]
w: The glo- ries of my God and King, The * tri- umphs of His grace!
w: To spread through all the earth a- broad The * ho- nors of Thy name.
w: 'Tis mu- sic in the sin- ner's ears, 'Tis * life, and health, and peace.
w: His blood can make the foul- est clean, His * blood a- vailed for me.
w: The mourn- ful, bro- ken hearts re- joice, The * hum- ble poor be- lieve.
w: By saints be- low and saints a- bove, The * church in earth and heav'n.
w: On my be- nig- hted soul He shone And * filled it with re- pose.
w: Pow'r with the Ho- ly Ghost re- ceived To * call the Sav- ior mine.
w: Me, me He loved, the Son of God, For * me, for me He died!
w: My par- don passed in heav'n I knew When * writ- ten on my heart.
w: Look, and be saved through faith a- lone, Be * jus- ti- fied by grace.
w: Saved is the sin- ner that be- lieves From * crimes as great as mine.
